{:db/id 17592186166866 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186166719 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e118393-2388-5add-b516-e565abe1e36a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to an Ellipse"}] :question/id #uuid "04c9673b-e4e5-508d-acc7-ea0888f2cf87" :question/math-academy-id "e-9578" :question/problem "![](images/d3/d3895bafe045f7e460887aee41bf390fdda753fed87eaab14f4a29ddb792267c.png)\n\nFind $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}y}{\\textrm{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $2$ and $4,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{2^2} + \\dfrac{y^2}{4^2} = 1 \\qquad \\Longrightarrow \\qquad \\dfrac{x^2}{4} + \\dfrac{y^2}{16} = 1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm d y}{\\textrm d x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{4}+\\frac{2y}{16}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{x}{2}+\\frac{y}{8}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{y}{8}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{4x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e118393-2388-5add-b516-e565abe1e36a" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186049699}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186167093 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e118393-2388-5add-b516-e565abe1e36a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b3ad7cd7-53ee-50c6-991d-7d73a0f6743a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2x}{3y}" :db/id 17592186163637} {:answer/id #uuid "bb3df2cb-6a20-5d32-8269-e7e4d022249d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4x}{9y}" :db/id 17592186163638} {:answer/id #uuid "0813c0d3-82a8-5058-a03d-c618284e99e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x}{2y}" :db/id 17592186163639} {:answer/id #uuid "46c3927c-367a-5b92-ab69-0a1993e45431" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9x}{4y}" :db/id 17592186163640} {:answer/id #uuid "7ebe77cd-3662-58ce-b781-4d6dd8b29dc6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4x}{9y}" :db/id 17592186163641}] :answer-field/id #uuid "5cd20f05-fcd1-55c1-8286-a5e170cba952" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186163636}] :question/id #uuid "feee00f3-146d-53ba-a889-b1572bbf7d4c" :question/math-academy-id "q-127362" :question/problem "![](images/f7/f74e1bfe8c53edb73d22633aa3bbf59f5046ebf793541dac8cbcf35127b72601.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{dy}{dx}$ for the ellipse shown above."} {:db/id 17592186167094 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e118393-2388-5add-b516-e565abe1e36a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b8de18c-3f57-5375-af7f-efa2e0197549" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3(y+1)}{4(x-2)}" :db/id 17592186507652} {:answer/id #uuid "a673094f-6307-5b33-92bf-06c740822bf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16(x-2)}{9(y+1)}" :db/id 17592186507832} {:answer/id #uuid "db7d24c3-d19d-5779-b9b1-949d29cf47df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9(y+1)}{16(x-2)}" :db/id 17592186507894} {:answer/id #uuid "f0580d29-12ed-56aa-ba70-461fe3aa6008" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16(x-2)}{9(y+1)}" :db/id 17592186507923} {:answer/id #uuid "f95d1962-8d93-5d37-a3ac-481ea9ea1974" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4(x-2)}{3(y+1)}" :db/id 17592186507935}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a673094f-6307-5b33-92bf-06c740822bf6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{16(x-2)}{9(y+1)}" :db/id 17592186507832} :answer-field/id #uuid "ae32260f-36b3-5a38-a8ce-a21db00f57c9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186163642}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "321fa992-8b54-51c4-9c6a-89b1f36a3444" :question/math-academy-id "q-127364" :question/problem "![](images/b5/b56ff4cb47d9b529762c6364eac2eed4b666c7ca9eab6f6ba7d3bc161387433e.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at $(2,-1)$ and has semiaxes $3$ and $4,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{4}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{16}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{16}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{9})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(y+1)^{2}}{16}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(x-2)}{9}+\\frac{2(y+1)}{16}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{y+1}{8}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2(x-2)}{9} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{16(x-2)}{9(y+1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186262783 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e118393-2388-5add-b516-e565abe1e36a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "193eadf3-4d9d-5560-876d-95d6202e9c93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{y}{2x}" :db/id 17592186260095} {:answer/id #uuid "35d44e75-ae76-5b88-839e-6d033a89f631" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x}{4y}" :db/id 17592186260357} {:answer/id #uuid "5f1dc785-7cef-5337-90f3-1ba825d33fc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4x}{y}" :db/id 17592186260694} {:answer/id #uuid "76364d2a-ee13-58e3-90a7-aedf8b7a207f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2x}{y}" :db/id 17592186260907} {:answer/id #uuid "85fa198d-352f-536a-a28b-55a7d967de78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y}{4x}" :db/id 17592186261038}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5f1dc785-7cef-5337-90f3-1ba825d33fc4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4x}{y}" :db/id 17592186260694} :answer-field/id #uuid "f89dbf13-8c69-578f-a637-7a5acc775b45" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186262554}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "adf3739c-b726-56b2-925a-36974745f33e" :question/math-academy-id "q-127511" :question/problem "![](images/c0/c0295c7cdc1abc16273efda842a0aa7a892ece2f5dda5e29f7baab25320b23ec.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $1$ and $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,{x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{2})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}) & =0 \\\\ 2x+\\frac{2y}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{y}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-2x \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{4x}{y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186262784 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e118393-2388-5add-b516-e565abe1e36a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1140d60d-8a60-5b24-9707-fdbbe10ee174" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9y}{25x}" :db/id 17592186260030} {:answer/id #uuid "4928b8e7-3c13-5270-9da7-dbed823cec42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5y}{3x}" :db/id 17592186260508} {:answer/id #uuid "898d463a-7dfd-5838-ad1a-295cc8ef06dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25y}{9x}" :db/id 17592186261076} {:answer/id #uuid "cd48c351-7d51-5019-b57c-50ccdbfa2e87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9x}{25y}" :db/id 17592186261684} {:answer/id #uuid "e37eac43-a53e-522f-a6fb-5b0bac1c7603" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3x}{5y}" :db/id 17592186261876}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "cd48c351-7d51-5019-b57c-50ccdbfa2e87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9x}{25y}" :db/id 17592186261684} :answer-field/id #uuid "00c0aa41-e415-529b-aa04-ad06f0391b13" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186262124}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4ab32aff-f9ee-5a7b-b7ab-1cf6d27aabda" :question/math-academy-id "q-127512" :question/problem "![](images/43/43e8ed1ee117ccd10f0e3aa03fc8db8ec1db6c076689e9072e1e22e048dfc279.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $5$ and $3,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{25}+\\frac{2y}{9}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2y}{9}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2x}{25} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{9x}{25y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186262785 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e118393-2388-5add-b516-e565abe1e36a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "183fee6d-7bac-5669-b5aa-f2ca1c2bd40e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{25x}{4y}" :db/id 17592186260087} {:answer/id #uuid "2282148e-42ae-5ff6-bce6-30eb16686d74" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5x}{2y}" :db/id 17592186260177} {:answer/id #uuid "916a9d4b-7d6d-5152-a204-c68e617838a9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5y}{2x}" :db/id 17592186261138} {:answer/id #uuid "9bcc7b58-ed39-578e-82a9-0c547be35fec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5x}{2y}" :db/id 17592186261225} {:answer/id #uuid "d7c686f5-6e36-5c65-8a51-b8412271e0e3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{25y}{4x}" :db/id 17592186261776}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "183fee6d-7bac-5669-b5aa-f2ca1c2bd40e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{25x}{4y}" :db/id 17592186260087} :answer-field/id #uuid "1a57a652-58c5-59d0-92fb-d161ba76dd70" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186262167}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "fb8ad6d7-f6da-5fbc-be48-a49f26e33603" :question/math-academy-id "q-127513" :question/problem "![](images/f8/f8effaf21270245ed6f8df63d2e430483756f47537b1c7325e88acc5286544db.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $2$ and $5,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{4}+\\frac{2y}{25}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2y}{25}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{25x}{4y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186262786 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e118393-2388-5add-b516-e565abe1e36a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2c1c1e34-b587-5bca-a469-20c953d57e6f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{3y}" :db/id 17592186260270} {:answer/id #uuid "693786d3-819f-5b02-b1be-af3f39567b51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{9y}" :db/id 17592186260794} {:answer/id #uuid "9090e1a2-9626-5a06-becc-3f269eff1a24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9x}{y}" :db/id 17592186261133} {:answer/id #uuid "a67e3b39-983b-5712-8fb5-9b1da10418c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3y}{x}" :db/id 17592186261326} {:answer/id #uuid "c9ba3065-ceff-5d5a-b70f-f705a5bbfc51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9y}{x}" :db/id 17592186261660}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "693786d3-819f-5b02-b1be-af3f39567b51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x}{9y}" :db/id 17592186260794} :answer-field/id #uuid "86e3dd0a-3fde-5ff0-95a9-90f1ef3e0463" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186262357}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9b971938-bd81-5d73-bed8-1323d79a80ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-127514" :question/problem "![](images/54/547b79b566d2914db4a63997cd5fc9f02dd1517b8dcd5e53cde8c07ac5ca05a2.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at the origin and has semiaxes $3$ and $1,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{1}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+{y}^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+{y}^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({y}^{2}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{9}+2y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2y\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2x}{9} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{9y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186262789 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e118393-2388-5add-b516-e565abe1e36a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4851ac26-61ba-5347-9f08-d47ae995e612" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+1}{4(y+1)}" :db/id 17592186260501} {:answer/id #uuid "4f4961c6-6f8c-5abb-ae07-f2b8f05a2801" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y-1}{4(x-1)}" :db/id 17592186260551} {:answer/id #uuid "73d79fd3-f240-55a0-b25f-2433c34e6adf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4(y+1)}{x+1}" :db/id 17592186260888} {:answer/id #uuid "a8dc3e16-f6aa-54b9-855f-a4bf2e902cc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x-1}{4(y-1)}" :db/id 17592186261353} {:answer/id #uuid "fcd86f62-82c8-517d-b725-1ed0ece0565b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4(x+1)}{y+1}" :db/id 17592186262087}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4851ac26-61ba-5347-9f08-d47ae995e612" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+1}{4(y+1)}" :db/id 17592186260501} :answer-field/id #uuid "e478fe35-cddc-5025-b3b3-364a777b1da3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186262528}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8af60131-dadd-5b8a-b5a0-d50b94e5f35b" :question/math-academy-id "q-127523" :question/problem "![](images/eb/ebef81911a434828ab94e643007d06b677538cdf0995198c7a065e35a8f81996.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at $(-1,-1)$ and has semiaxes $2$ and $1,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-(-1))^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-(-1))^{2}}{{1}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+(y+1)^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+(y+1)^{2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}((y+1)^{2}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(x+1)}{4}+2(y+1)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ 2(y+1)\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x+1}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x+1}{4(y+1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186262790 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e118393-2388-5add-b516-e565abe1e36a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4e42ef4c-5447-5bff-960b-4b0d7b21d724" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4(y-1)}{9x}" :db/id 17592186260539} {:answer/id #uuid "5c45f41e-d062-5f9f-b16d-79174ef52362" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3(y-1)}{2x}" :db/id 17592186260662} {:answer/id #uuid "9ec4a30f-fd49-5493-92c9-d0c013da0e11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3x}{2(y-1)}" :db/id 17592186261252} {:answer/id #uuid "c5590232-b5fa-5ba7-9564-1bf4158a2bf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9x}{4(y-1)}" :db/id 17592186261617} {:answer/id #uuid "d902d09a-c34e-56e1-b99d-14fc0f75c8a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4x}{9(y-1)}" :db/id 17592186261787}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5590232-b5fa-5ba7-9564-1bf4158a2bf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{9x}{4(y-1)}" :db/id 17592186261617} :answer-field/id #uuid "8fa189a6-0586-58c4-bdad-b279c7fe8ea4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186262377}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3bb11842-6e3d-5501-86bf-db20e32986e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-127525" :question/problem "![](images/eb/eb0fbc8f57621946a5ec5168e8c607d230269e0c6a64b4c86c835c110f0f6288.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at $(0,1)$ and has semiaxes $2$ and $3,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-0)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{9}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{9}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{9}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2x}{4}+\\frac{2(y-1)}{9}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(y-1)}{9}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x}{2} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{9x}{4(y-1)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186262791 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e118393-2388-5add-b516-e565abe1e36a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2265eb9b-3ab7-561c-9e8b-bbb0f82b1df6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{3y}{2(x-3)}" :db/id 17592186260173} {:answer/id #uuid "357f7559-50b2-593c-8d89-5de3d3f5f3d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2(x-3)}{3y}" :db/id 17592186260353} {:answer/id #uuid "398e1764-a4b7-5a3c-928e-904cdefd12f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4(y-3)}{9x}" :db/id 17592186260391} {:answer/id #uuid "7f214ada-9d01-5ad3-b18e-86c992bd8801" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9x}{4(y-3)}" :db/id 17592186260979} {:answer/id #uuid "d3513ebf-6544-564b-be5d-1eb3dcfba194" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4(x-3)}{9y}" :db/id 17592186261734}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d3513ebf-6544-564b-be5d-1eb3dcfba194" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4(x-3)}{9y}" :db/id 17592186261734} :answer-field/id #uuid "b98f98c2-9a67-5e94-9d12-ac8be15735e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186262460}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "32df6ca6-168d-529a-bf6d-352a5419e7a1" :question/math-academy-id "q-127526" :question/problem "![](images/e4/e4c39b409f6049a4fdead506c329d232820876c37ede9540adfeade2d7c1b9dc.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at $(3,0)$ and has semiaxes $3$ and $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{{3}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-0)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{9})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(x-3)}{9}+\\frac{2y}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{y}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{2(x-3)}{9} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{4(x-3)}{9y}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id 17592186503663 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1e118393-2388-5add-b516-e565abe1e36a" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4825a0cb-b3fb-5323-8a58-511f26bf6c7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{2(y-2)}{x+1}" :db/id 17592186503116} {:answer/id #uuid "6c6a63f8-ed2d-5275-9398-6d460d70e710" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{4(x+1)}{y-2}" :db/id 17592186503196} {:answer/id #uuid "7dfcca81-3430-5271-8cd0-80e5d2035124" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{y-2}{4(x+1)}" :db/id 17592186503241} {:answer/id #uuid "c5c781b7-f9f3-553f-b0be-cf3d3b1d44f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+1}{4(y-2)}" :db/id 17592186503376} {:answer/id #uuid "f7b72652-cf0b-559e-99bc-226911189b88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x+1}{2(y-2)}" :db/id 17592186503487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c5c781b7-f9f3-553f-b0be-cf3d3b1d44f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{x+1}{4(y-2)}" :db/id 17592186503376} :answer-field/id #uuid "88db5750-a4d8-5c4f-b26f-ef8a62130a02" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186503582}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "1e5b95a8-8914-5efe-a3ab-4b5dce1c8cbe" :question/math-academy-id "q-127521" :question/problem "![](images/e7/e74f96531b57a877b043ac4302adae6beef90dc24d64efc8e1a24b563e4738b7.png)\n\nFind $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}$ for the ellipse shown above." :question/worked-solution "Since our ellipse is centered at $(-1,2)$ and has semiaxes $4$ and $2,$ its equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-(-1))^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{{2}^{2}}=1\\,⟹\\,\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, to calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x},$ we use implicit differentiation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{16})+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{4}) & =0 \\\\ \\frac{2(x+1)}{16}+\\frac{2(y-2)}{4}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{y-2}{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x+1}{8} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{x+1}{4(y-2)}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Slope of the Tangent to an Ellipse"}